## Why

The managed quickstart stopped halfway: `brnrd account connect` paired the machine, then told a new user to discover and run `brnrd daemon install` separately. The native systemd/launchd service already existed; the guided path simply did not reach it.

## What changed

- `brnrd account connect` now pairs the account, installs the native user service, and starts it in one command;
- `--no-service` preserves foreground/container setups;
- the existing Linux linger controls are available on the combined command;
- README, getting-started, CLI reference, and bundled account-daemon docs now teach the one-command path;
- regression tests pin both the default durable path and the foreground escape.

This keeps the noun-first CLI decision intact: top-level `brnrd connect` remains retired rather than reappearing as a duplicate spelling.

